# Build output: patched copies, unpacked game files, logs.
build/
*.pck
*.pck.tmp

# Generated patched files. Regenerate with `python3 tools/build_patch.py`.
# The diffs are what belong in git; their output is rebuilt on the user's machine against the
# copy of the game they own. `**/` so nested folders are covered too — a patched `ui/CSS/*.gd`
# left in a commit would be a copy of the game.
patch/modified/**/*.gd
patch/modified/**/*.tscn
patch/modified/**/*.godot
patch/modified/**/*.import
# this project's own files, which do belong in git
!patch/modified/ai/**
!patch/modified/offline_compat/**
!patch/modified/Gamepad.gd

# Local-only art and music: this project's edits of the game's assets. They are in this repository
# on purpose (LEGAL.md explains the position), so nothing here is ignored — except the .import
# caches of anything else.

# No game files, ever.
*.stex
*.ctex
*.oggstr
*.mp3str
*.tpz
data.pck
YourOnlyMoveIsHUSTLE
YourOnlyMoveIsHUSTLE.exe
# ...except this project's own declared art and music and the import caches they need. A swapped
# .png without its matching .stex is a picture nobody sees, so both are committed on purpose; the
# .import caches of any other file stay out.
!localspot/**/*.stex
!localspot/**/*.md5

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Upstream originals: never committed. The diffs carry their own context and are applied to the
# user's own copy of the game instead. See LEGAL.md.
patch/original/
